The RNG is setting me up for another YASD, I can tell. In my third
game after the aforementioned black dragon disaster (playing Wiz
again), I found a *huge* general store on DL5 -- the largest I have
ever seen in my life. This was not to be believed. I brought my kitty
to it, and we cleaned out the entire place. It contained (in addition
to so much food I'd never have to worry about starving again, a cloak
of displacement, and so many potions I was burdened after we finished
robbing the place) a very highly-priced lamp. Fortunately I had found
an altar to Anhur on DL1, so I blessed some water, blessed the lamp,
and rubbed it. One turn later I had a +2 SDSM in my hands and could
not resist a chortle of glee. No disintegration deaths in this game!

It gets better. I proceeded to Minetown, where a store contained a
very expensive wand. I got my cat to steal it. Sure enough, it was a
wand of wishing -- *fully charged.* I almost fell over in my shock.
This kind of thing had never happened to me before. Four zaps later, I
had two scrolls of charging, +2 speed boots, a spellbook of identify,
and a bag of holding. I refrained from using the other wishes for the
moment on the grounds that they would make the rest of the game
horribly boring. I mean, who wants to be invulnerable already at
Minetown? (Though I have several things in mind, including magic
markers and a helm of brilliance.) In a way it almost seems like
cheating to use that many wishes so soon -- though they *did* come to
me completely honestly -- well, we'll see.

But anyway, I just *know* that this luck can't last. The RNG is
playing with my mind. How could I be so amazingly lucky and not suffer
for it later? :-)

